  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "In November 2026, Namit Malhotra confirmed the postponement, explaining that the filmmakers needed more time to complete the film given its scale.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1388181319:180"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "The ensemble cast includes Ranbir Kapoor, Yash in his Hindi film debut, Sai Pallavi, Ravi Dubey in his film debut, Anupam Kher, Lara Dutta, Shobana, Kajal Aggarwal and Rakul Preet Singh.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1388181319:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Ramayana: Part 1 is a 2026 Indian Hindi-language epic mythological film, directed by Nitesh Tiwari, who co-wrote the screenplay with Shridhar Raghavan.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1388181319:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:24Z",
      "text": "Ramayana: Part 1 stars Ranbir Kapoor, Yash, Sai Pallavi and Ravi Dubey; with music by Hans Zimmer and A. R. Rahman.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1388181319:starring",
        "wiki:box:1388181319:music"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "Released: 27 October 2026 (Academy Museum), 5 November 2026 (India). Box office, as Wikipedia records it: ₹1714.07 crore.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1388181319:released",
        "wiki:box:1388181319:box-office"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:43Z",
      "text": "On 30 April 2024, the second schedule commenced in Mumbai.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:film:1388181319:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:51Z",
      "text": "The article places the filming in Film City, Ayodhya and Mumbai.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:film:1388181319:1",
        "wiki:film:1388181319:2",
        "wiki:film:1388181319:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:01:01Z",
      "text": "Birthplaces are on record for 5 of the people credited, and 4 of them were born in India.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q108560:P19",
        "wd:Q16908467:P19",
        "wd:Q20081051:P19",
        "wd:Q7296622:P19",
        "wd:Q76364:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:01:09Z",
      "text": "Hans Zimmer was born further afield, in Frankfurt, Germany.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q76364:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:01:19Z",
      "text": "On 25 November 2026, 268,083 people read about the film, about 8 times the usual daily readership.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Ramayana:_Part_1:2026-11-25",
        "views:en:Ramayana:_Part_1:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:01:26Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 10 languages, and after English the most readers were in Chinese, with 318.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Ramayana:_Part_1:2026-11-25",
        "views:zh:羅摩衍那：傳奇崛起:2026-11-25"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:01:33Z",
      "text": "Each language glows where it is mainly spoken, and brighter colors mean more readers, though a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:zh:羅摩衍那：傳奇崛起:2026-11-25",
        "views:fr:Ramayana_:_L'Avènement_d'une_légende:2026-11-25",
